{
  "id": "ss.env.pan",
  "name": "Salt pan ground (SS)",
  "description": "Feelers' 128px floor for the Salt Pan: dark umber sand \u2014 `$sand`, a token between the field's soil and its rust \u2014 dark enough that the hive's magenta still has somewhere to go and the pale bodies of the pan roster read against it, warm enough to be baked rather than dead. What says salt is the veining: pale broken lines where the crust cracked and the salt dried white in the seams, a few thick patches of it, and pits with a lit lip where something came up through the floor. Rust flecks are the field's own, so the two grounds read as one world. Every coordinate is hand-listed so the tile is pixel-stable.",
